1
00:00:05,989 --> 00:00:09,559
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
"Great Detective Conan"
"Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi"

2
00:00:12,062 --> 00:00:12,629
Ran...

3
00:00:12,662 --> 00:00:14,131
Don't come in!

4
00:00:14,698 --> 00:00:15,899
What is it?

5
00:00:15,966 --> 00:00:17,901
It's okay, so come over here.

6
00:00:18,668 --> 00:00:20,470
I can't move...

7
00:00:20,737 --> 00:00:22,039
Eh?

8
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,208
This is...

9
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:27,611
Infra-red ray sensors?

10
00:00:27,978 --> 00:00:29,613
Shin'ichi...

11
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:32,215
I can't stand anymore.

12
00:00:32,749 --> 00:00:34,751
Ran, hang in there.

13
00:00:35,619 --> 00:00:36,520
"Careful, Explosion"

14
00:00:36,586 --> 00:00:37,821
Damn...

15
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:41,691
If I touch a sensor, there'll be a bang.

16
00:00:42,259 --> 00:00:43,960
This date was...

17
00:00:46,196 --> 00:00:48,065
"Beika City Bank
Safe-Deposit Boxes Floor"

18
00:00:56,673 --> 00:00:57,607
"Close"

19
00:01:03,213 --> 00:01:04,781
"Beika City Bank"

20
00:01:08,251 --> 00:01:10,987
"System Development Dept.
Sonoda Machiko"

21
00:01:11,088 --> 00:01:12,656
"The moment you report this to the police
This bank will blow up"

22
00:01:12,856 --> 00:01:14,558
"Blow up"

23
00:01:18,028 --> 00:01:21,064
"High School Student Detective
Kudo Shin'ichi"

24
00:01:21,298 --> 00:01:23,700
"Beika City Bank, Safe-Deposit Boxes Floor"
There's no mistake that's Sonoda Machiko-san?

25
00:01:23,767 --> 00:01:25,035
No mistake.

26
00:01:25,135 --> 00:01:28,939
That cell phone's Machiko-chan's.
I recognize the strap.

27
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:31,341
What sort of acquaintance
was Machiko-san to you?

28
00:01:31,475 --> 00:01:33,710
"Private Detective - Mori Kogoro"
Ran's computer school teacher.

29
00:01:33,777 --> 00:01:36,580
And my drinking buddy.
We weren't doing anything dirty. All wholesome...

30
00:01:36,613 --> 00:01:37,747
Oi!

31
00:01:37,881 --> 00:01:40,917
"Branch Manager - Emoto Takeo"
That computer school is a
subsidiary of our company.

32
00:01:41,017 --> 00:01:44,821
She held posts both here
and as a lecturer there.

33
00:01:44,955 --> 00:01:47,224
That ringtone!
That's definitely Machiko-chan's.

34
00:01:47,290 --> 00:01:49,493
"Mori Kogoro"
Machiko-chan, hang in there!

35
00:01:49,626 --> 00:01:50,594
It's true.

36
00:01:50,727 --> 00:01:52,295
Machiko-chan!

37
00:01:54,264 --> 00:01:58,135
"The moment you report this to the police,
this bank will blow up"

38
00:01:58,235 --> 00:02:00,504
Anyhow Branch Manager,
let's contact the police.

39
00:02:00,570 --> 00:02:01,905
Please wait a moment!

40
00:02:01,938 --> 00:02:04,574
What'll you do if it really does blow up?

41
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:08,912
Everyone here is saying
don't discuss this with the police.

42
00:02:09,446 --> 00:02:12,649
By the way, what are you doing here
at the bank, Sir?

43
00:02:12,849 --> 00:02:14,451
During the day today...

44
00:02:14,484 --> 00:02:16,987
"Ah, Machiko-chan!
What is it?"

45
00:02:17,053 --> 00:02:18,922
"Are you inviting me to a Go-kon?"

46
00:02:19,856 --> 00:02:21,091
"I'm sorry."

47
00:02:21,158 --> 00:02:25,162
"Truth is, I've gotten in some serious trouble
and was hoping to get your advice."

48
00:02:25,195 --> 00:02:28,465
"This can never be told to the police.
You cannot tell them."

49
00:02:28,598 --> 00:02:32,169
"So please, come to my desk at the bank."

50
00:02:32,302 --> 00:02:37,174
Thinking back on it now, this must have been
the reason she said not to tell them.

51
00:02:37,374 --> 00:02:41,077
And, when I guided Mori-san here...

52
00:02:41,378 --> 00:02:43,780
...for some reason these shutters were closed.

53
00:02:43,947 --> 00:02:45,549
Why do you say, "for some reason"?

54
00:02:45,649 --> 00:02:49,186
This shutter is
totally controlled by computer...

55
00:02:49,686 --> 00:02:52,322
...and isn't opened or shut at anytime
other than the scheduled hours.

56
00:02:52,389 --> 00:02:54,124
Oi, what does this mean?

57
00:02:54,224 --> 00:02:59,262
Most likely the criminal tampered with the
security system by hacking into its programming.

58
00:02:59,529 --> 00:03:02,933
What's more,
they were able to plant a device...

59
00:03:03,033 --> 00:03:05,602
...where the entire bank would blow up
the moment this panel is operated.

60
00:03:05,735 --> 00:03:08,371
An inside job crime...

61
00:03:08,572 --> 00:03:12,175
Each of the security camera videos
were checked on all the entrances and exits...

62
00:03:12,209 --> 00:03:16,780
...but no intruders were seen going
either in or out of this building.

63
00:03:17,247 --> 00:03:19,649
Who is currently left behind in this building?

64
00:03:19,716 --> 00:03:23,220
Us and 2 security guards...

65
00:03:23,653 --> 00:03:26,022
...and 3 others.

66
00:03:28,692 --> 00:03:31,027
"Assistant Branch Manager
Nimura Yuzo"

67
00:03:31,094 --> 00:03:33,330
"In Charge of Safe-deposit Boxes
Sakai Yoko"

68
00:03:33,463 --> 00:03:35,966
"Corporate Sales Division, Chief Clerk
Hasegawa Ryosuke"

69
00:03:45,709 --> 00:03:47,210
Which of you is the criminal?

70
00:03:47,277 --> 00:03:49,746
Sir, that kind of question is...

71
00:03:58,121 --> 00:04:00,523
Don't tell me it was all three of you?!

72
00:04:00,557 --> 00:04:01,758
- You're wrong!
- You're wrong!

73
00:04:02,292 --> 00:04:04,594
I alone killed her.

74
00:04:04,661 --> 00:04:06,062
- That's wrong!
- That's wrong!

75
00:04:06,229 --> 00:04:07,664
I did it.

76
00:04:07,731 --> 00:04:09,766
Wrong! I'm the criminal.

77
00:04:13,069 --> 00:04:14,571
Hello, Ran? Did it get there?

78
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:16,039
It's arrived, but...

79
00:04:16,139 --> 00:04:18,742
"Police Headquarters, Conference Room"
Say, what do you want done with
the photos you attached?

80
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:20,744
Have Detective Sato take a look at them.

81
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:24,414
She'll understand what I want analyzed
as soon as she reads the contents of the e-mail.

82
00:04:24,547 --> 00:04:26,883
"Shin'ichi's Childhood Friend - Mori Ran"
Yeah. Ah, wait, Shin'ichi!

83
00:04:27,384 --> 00:04:28,785
Geez...

84
00:04:28,885 --> 00:04:31,154
"MPD Investigation Unit One - Sato Miwako"
"MPD Investigation Unit One - Takagi Wataru"
"Photos"? What is this case about?

85
00:04:31,221 --> 00:04:35,992
I'm not sure, but I think he wants you
to have these photos analyzed.

86
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:38,194
"The moment you report this to the police
This bank will blow up"

87
00:04:38,928 --> 00:04:40,163
Blow up?!

88
00:04:40,196 --> 00:04:41,398
Get under a desk...

89
00:04:41,498 --> 00:04:42,565
Sato-san, hurry!
Ran-chan, you too...

90
00:04:42,632 --> 00:04:44,167
What are you doing?!
How shameful!

91
00:04:44,267 --> 00:04:45,902
I want you to tell the truth!

92
00:04:46,036 --> 00:04:49,139
I've done something terrible.
I didn't intend to kill her.

93
00:04:49,339 --> 00:04:52,842
She's dead. There's no doubt
since I'm telling you that I did it!

94
00:04:52,909 --> 00:04:54,210
Why are you lying...

95
00:04:54,311 --> 00:04:56,079
You're the one who's lying!

96
00:04:56,146 --> 00:04:58,748
I'm certainly the one who killed her.

97
00:04:58,815 --> 00:05:00,650
You're already too late.

98
00:05:00,884 --> 00:05:04,821
If you open the shutter here or if the
police start to move and this bank blows up...

99
00:05:04,854 --> 00:05:07,324
...you won't be able to recover her!

100
00:05:07,824 --> 00:05:09,359
Who put this up here?

101
00:05:12,796 --> 00:05:14,531
Ala, ala, ala?

102
00:05:14,698 --> 00:05:17,133
They're all denying it.

103
00:05:17,367 --> 00:05:20,103
Sir, let's divide them up for now
and listen to their circumstances.

104
00:05:20,203 --> 00:05:21,404
Oh.

105
00:05:21,905 --> 00:05:25,875
Let's put the screws on these guys
and kick their asses! Come!

106
00:05:30,613 --> 00:05:32,282
"Suspect 1
Assistant Branch Manager
Nimura Yuzo's Deposition"

107
00:05:32,382 --> 00:05:38,355
Truth is, I and Sonoda Machiko were trying
to keep our relationship quiet.

108
00:05:39,022 --> 00:05:40,657
You were lovers?

109
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:45,895
At first we mutually promised it would
just be a businesslike relationship...

110
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:51,234
...but recently Machiko had been saying
she couldn't endure that any longer...

111
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:52,602
"Divorce your wife."

112
00:05:52,635 --> 00:05:54,471
She was pressing me to marry her.

113
00:05:54,571 --> 00:05:55,939
"I told you, that's..."

114
00:05:56,072 --> 00:05:58,308
"I'll tell your wife EVERYTHING."

115
00:05:58,441 --> 00:05:59,976
"Stop it, I said..."

116
00:06:00,176 --> 00:06:01,811
"Wait... Ah!"

117
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:08,218
You're saying you killed her after reaching
the limits of her blind love for you?

118
00:06:08,651 --> 00:06:11,187
It was bound to be like this someday.

119
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:13,289
If I hadn't done that...

120
00:06:13,757 --> 00:06:16,326
...my family would have fallen apart.

121
00:06:17,394 --> 00:06:19,562
That's what I was thinking...

122
00:06:24,167 --> 00:06:28,171
By the way, was it you who
put up that poster, Nimura-san?

123
00:06:29,339 --> 00:06:32,175
I don't know... anything about that.

124
00:06:32,876 --> 00:06:34,711
"Suspect 2
In Charge of Safe-deposit Boxes
Sakai Yoko's Deposition"

125
00:06:35,078 --> 00:06:37,614
That woman was the subject of dark rumors.

126
00:06:38,348 --> 00:06:40,884
There were dark rumors about Machiko-chan?

127
00:06:43,186 --> 00:06:45,789
That she was embezzling from the company.

128
00:06:46,055 --> 00:06:49,259
That she was opening safe-deposit boxes
without authorization from the users...

129
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:51,995
...and taking out any precious goods.

130
00:06:52,228 --> 00:06:56,132
They were collateral
for her financing schemes.

131
00:06:56,566 --> 00:06:58,435
She would make investments using them...

132
00:06:58,535 --> 00:07:03,306
...and, once she had made a profit,
would return the goods...

133
00:07:03,473 --> 00:07:05,975
...keeping the profits for herself.

134
00:07:09,045 --> 00:07:10,680
That's nothing to joke about!

135
00:07:10,747 --> 00:07:14,350
The career I had built up for myself
was being ruined by that little girl!

136
00:07:14,484 --> 00:07:18,888
That's why it was necessary for me to
convince her to stop before this became serious.

137
00:07:19,389 --> 00:07:21,624
Since you have to take responsibility
for your subordinates...

138
00:07:21,724 --> 00:07:24,594
...you could have been fired as well, right?

139
00:07:24,894 --> 00:07:27,831
So you tried everything that you could.

140
00:07:27,964 --> 00:07:33,036
Today as expected, she was returning goods
she had taken without authorization.

141
00:07:35,438 --> 00:07:38,608
"Ala. I don't want to hear
any more excuses."

142
00:07:38,908 --> 00:07:40,276
"Before you lose this bank's trust..."

143
00:07:40,343 --> 00:07:42,946
"Before they lose trust in ME?"

144
00:07:43,546 --> 00:07:45,582
"What a laugh."

145
00:07:45,782 --> 00:07:49,853
"Should I dial 110 and expose myself?"

146
00:07:50,153 --> 00:07:51,187
"Wait..."

147
00:07:55,492 --> 00:07:57,961
If I had let her get away like that,
it could have gotten serious for me...

148
00:07:58,061 --> 00:07:59,496
That's what I was thinking...

149
00:07:59,696 --> 00:08:01,498
And she had realized that.

150
00:08:02,065 --> 00:08:04,567
Did you put up that poster?

151
00:08:05,335 --> 00:08:06,736
No.

152
00:08:07,103 --> 00:08:10,974
But, I don't think it's a bluff.

153
00:08:11,107 --> 00:08:12,408
What?

154
00:08:12,675 --> 00:08:15,311
She was an excellent System Engineer.

155
00:08:15,411 --> 00:08:18,448
With this system, intruders couldn't get past.

156
00:08:18,515 --> 00:08:19,983
Moreover...

157
00:08:20,316 --> 00:08:22,919
Even I don't know what
those safe-deposit boxes contain.

158
00:08:23,019 --> 00:08:24,554
If you checked all of them...

159
00:08:24,654 --> 00:08:28,424
...I couldn't deny the possibility that
one of them contains a bomb.

160
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:31,694
Then...

161
00:08:32,328 --> 00:08:33,429
...it was Machiko who put it up?

162
00:08:33,496 --> 00:08:35,798
That's what I think.

163
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:38,568
"Suspect 3
Chief of Corporate Sales
Hasegawa Ryosuke's Deposition"

164
00:08:38,635 --> 00:08:41,638
"if you do as I say, you can make
a lot of money..." she said.

165
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:43,339
But...

166
00:08:44,073 --> 00:08:48,578
...an emergency broke out,
so she wanted my cooperation.

167
00:08:48,778 --> 00:08:50,513
Emergency?

168
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:54,317
She was taking precious goods
from the safe-deposit boxes...

169
00:08:54,751 --> 00:08:56,886
...and using them to make money...

170
00:08:58,087 --> 00:09:00,924
Our boss, Sakai-san,
had gotten wind of that...

171
00:09:01,457 --> 00:09:03,259
And...

172
00:09:03,726 --> 00:09:06,095
"I want you to kill me."

173
00:09:06,863 --> 00:09:08,097
"Eh?"

174
00:09:09,198 --> 00:09:11,301
"Of course, it's just a little play."

175
00:09:12,201 --> 00:09:13,369
"A play?"

176
00:09:13,503 --> 00:09:17,674
"Truth is, I'm borrowing something
right now for the collateral I need."

177
00:09:18,074 --> 00:09:22,512
"An emerald necklace currently worth
about 260 million yen."

178
00:09:23,246 --> 00:09:24,981
"260 million yen?"

179
00:09:25,148 --> 00:09:28,918
"The Middle East ambassador of
the Cairid Kingdom deposited it."

180
00:09:29,018 --> 00:09:32,755
"That necklace is something I've taken out
of the safe-deposit box for right now."

181
00:09:33,022 --> 00:09:37,093
"However tomorrow, because his
business plans changed suddenly..."

182
00:09:37,193 --> 00:09:41,564
"...the ambassador wants to take his
emerald necklace out before returning home."

183
00:09:41,898 --> 00:09:45,501
"But I can't return the emerald that quickly."

184
00:09:47,537 --> 00:09:49,072
"You understand, right?"

185
00:09:49,572 --> 00:09:52,408
"If that safe-deposit box is opened,
it's over for us."

186
00:09:52,875 --> 00:09:56,145
"That's why before then,
some big incident needs to occur..."

187
00:09:56,245 --> 00:10:00,416
"...so that the shutter is closed
and can't be opened."

188
00:10:00,817 --> 00:10:02,585
"How?!"

189
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:07,857
The ambassador has to return to his home
because he can't change his schedule.

190
00:10:08,157 --> 00:10:09,592
When the time comes...

191
00:10:09,726 --> 00:10:12,996
...he'll have no choice but to
return home for the time being.

192
00:10:13,529 --> 00:10:16,966
In other words,
that poster is nothing but a bluff?

193
00:10:19,802 --> 00:10:23,773
She would gain time because...

194
00:10:24,941 --> 00:10:28,277
...they'd be too afraid to make it a
police matter and too scared to open the shutter.

195
00:10:29,078 --> 00:10:32,915
Then, you're saying... she's still alive?

196
00:10:32,982 --> 00:10:34,550
That's right.

197
00:10:35,652 --> 00:10:40,657
She took sleeping pills
and is pretending to be a corpse.

198
00:10:42,492 --> 00:10:44,894
By the time they wear off...

199
00:10:45,495 --> 00:10:49,532
In other words, her plan is to
regain consciousness around 9 a.m...

200
00:10:49,732 --> 00:10:52,368
...after the ambassador to Japan has left.

201
00:10:52,769 --> 00:10:54,370
And...

202
00:10:54,671 --> 00:10:59,242
...once she inputs the password,
nothing will happen.

203
00:11:00,243 --> 00:11:04,547
Then she's the only one
who knows the password.

204
00:11:05,148 --> 00:11:07,483
She's a scary woman.

205
00:11:08,184 --> 00:11:10,086
If I hadn't gone along like this...

206
00:11:10,820 --> 00:11:13,856
...it wouldn't be possible to stop her crimes.

207
00:11:15,158 --> 00:11:18,828
Hasegawa-san, you were going to
play your part in Machiko-san's plan...

208
00:11:19,028 --> 00:11:23,366
...wait for her to return the emeralds
and then file a complaint?

209
00:11:23,533 --> 00:11:26,869
Afterwards,
I'd explain everything to the police.

210
00:11:27,003 --> 00:11:29,572
What?! Machiko-chan is alive?

211
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:32,742
That's according to Hasegawa-san's story.

212
00:11:33,209 --> 00:11:35,578
Machiko-chan! Hang in there!

213
00:11:35,645 --> 00:11:37,046
I'll save you!

214
00:11:37,180 --> 00:11:40,183
But Sir, it's all contradictory.

215
00:11:40,850 --> 00:11:42,318
Contradictory?!

216
00:11:43,553 --> 00:11:46,956
Both Sakai-san and Hasegawa-san said
that Machiko-san was embezzling.

217
00:11:47,023 --> 00:11:48,791
"She was embezzling from the company."

218
00:11:49,058 --> 00:11:53,496
"She was taking precious goods from the
safe-deposit boxes and making money from them..."

219
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:56,799
So the probability she was embezzling is high.

220
00:11:56,966 --> 00:12:01,771
But, if as Hasegawa-san has said
and Machiko-san is playing dead...

221
00:12:02,772 --> 00:12:06,209
...then that deposition contradicts
what Sakai-san said about killing her.

222
00:12:06,342 --> 00:12:09,846
Even though Sakai-san herself
is saying she did kill her.

223
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:11,547
"Divorce her."

224
00:12:12,715 --> 00:12:15,651
On the other hand, Nimura says
he killed her out of blind passion.

225
00:12:15,885 --> 00:12:17,286
What on earth is going on?!

226
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:20,256
You normally wouldn't say you were
the one doing that.

227
00:12:20,389 --> 00:12:26,329
Between the three of them, there must be
something the criminal had found convenient.

228
00:12:27,897 --> 00:12:30,867
Something the criminal had found
convenient to them!

229
00:12:32,635 --> 00:12:34,203
What is it?

230
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:40,009
Oh Ran, find out anything?

231
00:12:40,276 --> 00:12:42,011
Shin'ichi, listen closely.

232
00:12:42,111 --> 00:12:44,814
There's a red mark showing up on
Machiko-san's leg.

233
00:12:44,947 --> 00:12:46,816
Most likely that's...

234
00:12:47,116 --> 00:12:49,352
Eh? And?

235
00:12:51,354 --> 00:12:52,822
Got it.

236
00:13:00,663 --> 00:13:03,199
Oi! Where are you going?
Boy detective!

237
00:13:03,266 --> 00:13:04,500
Oi!

238
00:13:04,767 --> 00:13:08,337
"System Development Department"

239
00:13:12,074 --> 00:13:14,143
It hasn't gone into Sleep mode.

240
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:15,878
"Wait in the basement safe-deposit box room
If I don't show up, e-mail me here"

241
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:19,982
"Machiko"

242
00:13:21,984 --> 00:13:27,123
There's something unusual about Sir's
drinking buddy Machiko-san's e-mail address...

243
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:35,264
Damn!

244
00:13:35,598 --> 00:13:38,134
Just a little more...

245
00:13:39,936 --> 00:13:41,771
Sir, what are you doing?

246
00:13:41,871 --> 00:13:45,341
Well, I thought I'd get that cell phone.

247
00:13:45,474 --> 00:13:48,477
I thought we might be able
to find something out with it.

248
00:13:48,711 --> 00:13:50,446
Where did you get that?

249
00:13:50,613 --> 00:13:53,082
I grabbed a brace from
one of the plants over there.

250
00:14:15,204 --> 00:14:17,373
This is wonderful, Sir.

251
00:14:17,506 --> 00:14:19,375
This is great, Sir!

252
00:14:19,475 --> 00:14:21,377
This had a hand in it.

253
00:14:21,477 --> 00:14:23,746
Huh? Huh, huh, huh?

254
00:14:24,046 --> 00:14:27,383
Really? That's right, isn't it?
I knew it!

255
00:14:27,617 --> 00:14:33,422
For this great detective, Mori Kogoro, every
sort of closed-room trick is but child's play.

256
00:14:35,658 --> 00:14:37,126
And? What's the trick?

257
00:14:37,226 --> 00:14:39,128
I'll explain it later.

258
00:14:44,066 --> 00:14:45,134
Huh?

259
00:14:45,201 --> 00:14:46,569
An explosion?!

260
00:14:46,636 --> 00:14:48,838
Didn't a detonator just start?

261
00:14:49,005 --> 00:14:50,206
I thought so.

262
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:51,774
What did you just think?!

263
00:14:51,841 --> 00:14:53,175
What's this about, boy detective?

264
00:14:53,276 --> 00:14:56,412
The cell phone at
Machiko-san's foot isn't reacting.

265
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,482
But...

266
00:15:01,884 --> 00:15:05,021
...an e-mail ringtone can
be heard from inside there.

267
00:15:05,187 --> 00:15:09,959
That means there's another
cell phone somewhere in there.

268
00:15:10,026 --> 00:15:11,727
Where in there?!

269
00:15:11,894 --> 00:15:15,298
All of the mysteries are hidden in this number.

270
00:15:16,499 --> 00:15:19,635
Fool! It'll explode!
That's dangerous!

271
00:15:36,719 --> 00:15:39,922
This is regrettable, Machiko-san.

272
00:15:40,589 --> 00:15:43,492
Ma... Machiko-chan!

273
00:15:43,592 --> 00:15:45,895
Unfortunately, she's dead.

274
00:15:50,199 --> 00:15:51,934
Poor thing...

275
00:15:54,804 --> 00:15:57,506
Oi! She wasn't strangled.

276
00:15:57,707 --> 00:16:00,176
Then what on earth
was the cause of her death?

277
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:02,778
I'll explain that later.

278
00:16:04,180 --> 00:16:06,816
Sir, where's that sound coming from?

279
00:16:14,623 --> 00:16:17,560
From here! I can hear it here!

280
00:16:18,027 --> 00:16:20,930
Only one part is open.
Just like I thought.

281
00:16:20,997 --> 00:16:23,933
Sir! Machiko-san should have
the master key. Search her!

282
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,201
Yeah!

283
00:16:29,605 --> 00:16:31,941
Boy detective, I have it!

284
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:43,986
I know, Sir.

285
00:16:45,488 --> 00:16:47,423
What the one and only...

286
00:16:48,657 --> 00:16:51,527
...sad truth is.

287
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:54,797
I know who the criminal is.

288
00:16:54,864 --> 00:16:56,699
Who is the criminal?!

289
00:16:56,799 --> 00:16:59,435
I will explain that in order.

290
00:17:00,636 --> 00:17:01,971
Sonoda-kun...

291
00:17:02,138 --> 00:17:03,839
Sonoda-kun, this is enough.

292
00:17:03,973 --> 00:17:06,375
It's time to stop your play.

293
00:17:09,078 --> 00:17:11,680
Outsiders have learned this much about it.

294
00:17:11,947 --> 00:17:14,683
It's not possible for you to hide from
your crimes any longer.

295
00:17:14,717 --> 00:17:17,386
Sonoda Machiko-san is completely dead.

296
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:18,821
Eh?!

297
00:17:19,388 --> 00:17:21,123
That's not possible!

298
00:17:25,294 --> 00:17:26,829
That will contact the police!

299
00:17:26,896 --> 00:17:28,164
It'll explode!

300
00:17:28,230 --> 00:17:29,698
Don't worry!

301
00:17:29,799 --> 00:17:33,669
We've already opened it once before.

302
00:17:34,403 --> 00:17:38,007
It didn't explode,
nor did it contact the police.

303
00:17:38,107 --> 00:17:41,177
Someone's been tampering with the system.

304
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:50,086
No...

305
00:17:52,688 --> 00:17:54,557
What is this about?

306
00:17:55,191 --> 00:17:59,261
The presumption of this bomb warning...

307
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:03,432
...was that it was to camouflage that
Sonoda Machiko-san was feigning to be a corpse.

308
00:18:03,566 --> 00:18:04,834
In other words...

309
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:09,805
...this poster and Machiko-san
being murdered for embezzling...

310
00:18:09,872 --> 00:18:11,874
...are two separate things.

311
00:18:12,141 --> 00:18:13,776
Separate things?

312
00:18:13,909 --> 00:18:15,144
That's right.

313
00:18:15,611 --> 00:18:18,414
Half a year ago, Machiko-san,
who knew all about computers...

314
00:18:18,547 --> 00:18:22,651
...was commissioned by this bank's senior
management to perform a top secret mission.

315
00:18:22,952 --> 00:18:24,753
Top secret mission?!

316
00:18:24,887 --> 00:18:27,356
In order to stop a fraud from
within the bank...

317
00:18:27,456 --> 00:18:32,528
...her duty was to hack into the computers of
the entire bank staff and keep an eye on them.

318
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:36,398
To prove the truth about this...

319
00:18:36,398 --> 00:18:39,735
...Machiko-san hid something
in this safe-deposit box in advance.

320
00:18:39,768 --> 00:18:41,137
That was...

321
00:18:43,005 --> 00:18:44,740
...this diary.

322
00:18:45,141 --> 00:18:50,846
This diary contains an exchange
of e-mails between two people.

323
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:52,648
These are...

324
00:18:52,815 --> 00:18:56,185
...the exchanges between
Sakai-san and Nimura-san.

325
00:18:56,585 --> 00:19:00,689
The ones who removed the ambassador's
emerald from the safe-deposit box...

326
00:19:00,856 --> 00:19:02,892
...was you two, wasn't it?

327
00:19:03,792 --> 00:19:06,862
You two took the necklace out...

328
00:19:07,029 --> 00:19:11,200
...and then approached Machiko-san
with a plan to camouflage it.

329
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,936
"Please! We'll do this!"

330
00:19:14,036 --> 00:19:17,706
"If this is exposed, it'll not only mean the end
of the bank but an international incident as well!"

331
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:21,343
"Sonoda-kun. You're the only one
we can rely on. Help us!"

332
00:19:21,443 --> 00:19:24,780
"I still have two little children. Please!"

333
00:19:24,847 --> 00:19:27,917
"Hey! If you can just hold him off
until tomorrow, we'll put it all back!"

334
00:19:28,017 --> 00:19:32,087
"Besides, once the emerald is returned,
no one will suffer any loss or be hurt."

335
00:19:32,221 --> 00:19:33,822
"Sonoda-kun!"

336
00:19:35,291 --> 00:19:38,093
Machiko-san, following your request...

337
00:19:38,227 --> 00:19:44,200
...bypassed the security system,
changed the password and closed the shutter.

338
00:19:47,203 --> 00:19:48,938
"I'm counting on you."

339
00:19:53,475 --> 00:19:59,148
And, leaving this poster so the shutter wouldn't be
opened until after the ambassador to Japan had left...

340
00:19:59,215 --> 00:20:01,884
...you testified to having killed Machiko-san.

341
00:20:02,017 --> 00:20:05,554
But...
But we really didn't kill her!

342
00:20:05,721 --> 00:20:07,756
It's true! We didn't kill her!

343
00:20:07,890 --> 00:20:10,759
Because Machiko-chan was just faking
she had been killed...

344
00:20:10,926 --> 00:20:14,763
...you thought you'd be safe in saying
you had killed her, didn't you?

345
00:20:15,464 --> 00:20:19,835
Not wanting the ambassador
to enter the safe-deposit box room...

346
00:20:19,969 --> 00:20:25,674
...you'd need a credible murder case
as well as a bomb warning to do that.

347
00:20:26,408 --> 00:20:27,776
Nimura-san.

348
00:20:27,977 --> 00:20:32,081
Your talk about having an affair with
Machiko-san was all nonsense, wasn't it?

349
00:20:32,381 --> 00:20:36,719
Rather than adultery, you were in debt
for tens of millions of yen.

350
00:20:37,186 --> 00:20:39,688
Did she write such things?

351
00:20:40,289 --> 00:20:45,594
Therefore, in order to repay the debt,
you joined forces with Sakai-san, didn't you?

352
00:20:47,363 --> 00:20:48,931
Were you out of your mind, Sakai?!

353
00:20:48,998 --> 00:20:50,733
I didn't know about this!

354
00:20:50,799 --> 00:20:53,636
You two are criminal embezzlers.

355
00:20:53,769 --> 00:20:58,540
And, the criminal who murdered
Machiko-san was...

356
00:21:00,009 --> 00:21:03,512
And, the criminal who murdered
Machiko-san was...

357
00:21:05,147 --> 00:21:08,183
...you, Hasegawa-san.

358
00:21:11,153 --> 00:21:12,721
What are you suggesting?

359
00:21:12,888 --> 00:21:17,926
In this diary,
you were written up about separately.

360
00:21:18,727 --> 00:21:20,696
As her lover...

361
00:21:20,896 --> 00:21:24,500
...Machiko-san wrote about her feelings for you
and her dreams of the future with you.

362
00:21:24,667 --> 00:21:28,904
You and Machiko-chan were engaged, right?

363
00:21:29,638 --> 00:21:34,810
You were engaged, but you were seeing
another woman on the side as well.

364
00:21:35,277 --> 00:21:38,314
A client company's daughter, isn't it?

365
00:21:39,148 --> 00:21:42,251
But, Machiko-san believed in you.

366
00:21:42,284 --> 00:21:48,257
That's why you were the only one she discussed
Sakai-san and Nimura-san's fraud request with.

367
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:51,126
Here's what's written.

368
00:21:52,628 --> 00:21:54,096
"I'm so happy."

369
00:21:54,229 --> 00:22:00,102
"He says we'll go to the police and have
Sakai-san and Nimura-san prosecuted."

370
00:22:01,770 --> 00:22:03,639
Yet even so, you betrayed her.

371
00:22:03,739 --> 00:22:05,274
What's more, in the worst way.

372
00:22:05,341 --> 00:22:06,842
Hold on there!

373
00:22:07,409 --> 00:22:09,478
This is just your own,
selfish line of reasoning.

374
00:22:09,611 --> 00:22:13,749
Thing is, when I got here,
the shutter had already been closed!

375
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:17,052
How could I possibly have killed her?

376
00:22:17,219 --> 00:22:18,654
You!

377
00:22:19,488 --> 00:22:21,657
I'll show you how right now!

378
00:22:26,829 --> 00:22:30,966
On Machiko-san's corpse,
there's a small red bleed mark.

379
00:22:31,734 --> 00:22:35,037
Machiko-san wasn't strangled...

380
00:22:35,804 --> 00:22:38,006
She was poisoned.

381
00:22:40,542 --> 00:22:46,348
You hid a blowgun disguised as
a brace hidden here...

382
00:22:46,715 --> 00:22:48,984
...in this shrub pot!

383
00:23:08,570 --> 00:23:14,143
Most likely the dart was tipped with
a powerful nerve poison.

384
00:23:15,043 --> 00:23:17,646
In order to kill her this way...

385
00:23:17,746 --> 00:23:24,219
...you'd need to know in advance Machiko-san was
playing dead here from having taken sleeping pills.

386
00:23:24,386 --> 00:23:27,456
Moreover, since the shutter was down...

387
00:23:27,623 --> 00:23:30,492
...you could testify that you
couldn't have killed her.

388
00:23:30,559 --> 00:23:35,597
Furthermore, the only person
who could use this secret room was...

389
00:23:36,231 --> 00:23:38,033
In other words...

390
00:23:39,868 --> 00:23:43,739
...that could only mean you, Hasegawa-san.

391
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:49,445
That's nothing but speculation.

392
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:53,048
It's not speculation!

393
00:23:53,248 --> 00:23:55,851
I'm MPD Investigation Unit One's, Sato.

394
00:23:56,018 --> 00:23:57,586
I'm Takagi of the same.

395
00:23:57,686 --> 00:23:59,822
We had an analysis done of
the photo of the corpse.

396
00:23:59,888 --> 00:24:03,325
From the circumstances of the corpse,
it's almost certain to be poison.

397
00:24:10,132 --> 00:24:15,571
I just sent an e-mail to the address
shown on Machiko-san's desk computer.

398
00:24:16,038 --> 00:24:21,310
But that isn't her cell phone that's ringing;
it's a different one.

399
00:24:22,444 --> 00:24:24,313
What are you getting at?

400
00:24:24,813 --> 00:24:26,582
Please listen closely.

401
00:24:26,815 --> 00:24:31,253
You should know where
that ringing is calling from.

402
00:24:32,287 --> 00:24:34,022
I don't know.

403
00:24:34,389 --> 00:24:36,658
0924...

404
00:24:37,459 --> 00:24:39,328
Does that ring any bells?

405
00:24:44,466 --> 00:24:47,636
Machiko-san made a gesture here
of her faith in you...

406
00:24:47,703 --> 00:24:52,307
...when she followed
Sakai-san's request to play dead.

407
00:24:56,478 --> 00:25:00,015
She believed you would return here,
accuse those two of embezzlement...

408
00:25:00,249 --> 00:25:03,218
...and then bring her back to normal...

409
00:25:03,418 --> 00:25:07,256
But you used her love.

410
00:25:07,489 --> 00:25:10,392
Taking advantage that she was playing dead...

411
00:25:10,659 --> 00:25:13,128
...you killed her.

412
00:25:17,833 --> 00:25:23,005
Tomorrow, September 24th,
is your birthday, isn't it?

413
00:25:26,241 --> 00:25:28,644
The password which opens this shutter...

414
00:25:28,844 --> 00:25:32,848
...is also the number of your birthday, "0924."

415
00:25:37,753 --> 00:25:39,688
Don't spout nonsense.

416
00:25:40,322 --> 00:25:44,660
Machiko-chan was only going to play dead,
but you didn't have to intentionally kill her!

417
00:25:45,761 --> 00:25:49,998
To say nothing that you shouldn't use a bombing
trick to go ahead and kill someone yourself!

418
00:25:51,366 --> 00:25:55,237
Machiko-san, after they had been successfully
charged with embezzling...

419
00:25:55,437 --> 00:26:00,709
...wanted to give you this cell phone as
a present from out of this safe-deposit box.

420
00:26:01,877 --> 00:26:05,447
The e-mail address for
this cell phone present...

421
00:26:06,081 --> 00:26:11,987
...is a combination of your birthday,
"September 24th"...

422
00:26:12,254 --> 00:26:15,591
...and your name, "Ryosuke."

423
00:26:29,237 --> 00:26:31,807
"As now, and forever more
I will love you
Machiko"

424
00:26:31,940 --> 00:26:35,744
"As now, and forever more..."

425
00:26:36,178 --> 00:26:38,547
"...I will love you."

426
00:26:38,847 --> 00:26:40,148
"Machiko."

427
00:26:50,092 --> 00:26:51,893
"Happy birthday"

428
00:27:03,105 --> 00:27:05,407
"Happy birthday."

429
00:27:12,014 --> 00:27:13,615
Machiko-chan...

430
00:27:14,016 --> 00:27:15,617
Machiko-chan...

431
00:27:16,985 --> 00:27:21,223
...believed in a worthless person like you...

432
00:27:21,456 --> 00:27:23,725
...until the very end!

433
00:27:24,326 --> 00:27:27,229
Why did you have to kill her,
you scum!

434
00:27:32,734 --> 00:27:34,536
Machiko...

435
00:27:36,038 --> 00:27:38,473
This was far too sad...

436
00:27:39,708 --> 00:27:41,443
Hasegawa-san...

437
00:27:51,253 --> 00:27:55,323
"Happy birthday"

438
00:28:06,568 --> 00:28:07,669
"Birthday"

439
00:28:10,872 --> 00:28:12,941
"Birthday"

440
00:28:17,913 --> 00:28:19,081
Ran!

441
00:28:24,186 --> 00:28:25,487
Ran?

442
00:28:30,358 --> 00:28:32,394
I see...

443
00:28:36,865 --> 00:28:38,767
I know now.

444
00:28:39,301 --> 00:28:42,637
Just why we are trapped in this room.

445
00:28:44,272 --> 00:28:46,575
The criminal who did all this...

446
00:28:48,677 --> 00:28:50,045
Ran...

447
00:28:50,245 --> 00:28:52,047
...it was you.

448
00:28:55,217 --> 00:28:57,219
"Ran is dead?!"

449
00:29:06,828 --> 00:29:09,230
"Finally, Next Week
The Shocking Final Episode!"

